    "mergeable": true,
    "draft": true,
    "body": "Diameter consumers need fragment flags, unconsumed oversized notifications, explicit per-message metadata, and cancellation that cannot outlive buffer ownership. This adds opt-in immutable message mode with ReadEvent/WriteMsgContext, context-aware resolution/dial, mutable deadlines and typed parsing of five existing Linux SCTP notifications. Nil Messages preserves legacy stream/callback behavior; message mode rejects mixed legacy I/O and setup callbacks.\n\nThe candidate remains pure Go on Go 1.26+, with no protocol state or persistence. Tests cover native long SEND_FAILED retry, address/partial/shutdown events, deadline/cancel/close boundaries and accept-option failures. The resource ledger declares a bounded single-reader/single-writer integration policy; its 8 KiB logical reserve is not an RSS guarantee. Keyed SocketConfig literals are required for source compatibility with the new field.\n\nValidation on the exact source tree: 315 native tests/subtests/fuzz seeds/examples, zero skips; the full local release script including 10 shuffled race rounds, checkptr, low-GC race and five 1,000,000-execution fuzz targets; README examples; six downstream compile targets; six architecture test builds; and a deterministic 430-file offline module installed by an independent real-SCTP consumer without replace. The existing remote native/Go/architecture/required-namespace matrix is required on this PR. No release notes, tag, merge or publication are requested by this draft.\n\nThis is the incremental diameterkit U2–U5 candidate based on 62ad388. The independent upstream v1 redesign and unrelated working-tree changes are excluded.",
    "title": "Add context-aware SCTP message I/O and typed notifications",
